 visualize  the long encoding rnas of interest in  cancer cells and tissues  this is another example of how  we can use different probes to identify  long encoding rnas  that are significant in a particular  malignancy  here you can use four different probes  in four different tumors  and you can appreciate the different uh  pattern of expression of  each of these long non-coding rnas where  we're in the gas 5-long non-coding rnas  expressed in breast cancer  shows both nuclear and cytoplasmic  expression  whereas the mallet one long non-coding  rna  shows specifically nuclear expression in  this lung cancer tumor  so with our technology you can get that  subcellular localization  of targets like these long encoding rnas  which can be significant in  understanding their function  in tumor growth and progression  so i want to take the remainder of the  time to talk about  a very exciting um collaboration  between acd biotechnic and nanostring  technology  where we have combined our technologies  in a single workflow  to give you highly plexed spatial  analysis with morphological context  early scope is now a part of the geomax  dsp workflow where rna scope can be used  as a molecular  guide to direct the dsp uh the geomex  csp  on specific areas of the tumor which can  then be profiled  using the dsp quantified using the  encounter  and then targets of interest can be  validated using  rna scope on ethereal section  so this is a workflow which we believe  can help  address several questions for immuno  oncology research  and this is especially significant for  samples  with high heterogeneity  we wanted to show that this particular  workflow  can be made applicable for an actual  uh study within a lung cancer tumor  sample  so we've decided to investigate the new  cell infiltration and the expression of  associated cytokines  in the tumor microenvironment  so the first step is to identify regions  of interest  using specific early scope probes the  second step as i mentioned is to perform  the digital spatial profiling using the  geomets  on these identified regions of interest  and then the third step is to validate  or confirm the data  that you get from your geomix dsp again  with that  single cell and single uh molecule  resolution  with rna scope so to show the  applicability of this technology  uh we decided to use  the cd3 and cd19 rna scope probes  to interrogate this lung cancer tumor  sample  and thought that different regions of  this lung cancer tumor  had varying degree of cd19 and cd3  expression  some regions had higher degree of cd19  expression  or some regions in high degree of cd3  expression  and this indicates the differential  expression  or differential levels of immune cell  infiltration  within this lung cancer tumor  so the 24 regions of entrance that were  identified  were a mix of high pd3 high  and moderate expression of both targets  after identifying these 24 regions of  interest  they were then analyzed using the  geomets dsp  the geometry panel that we chose is the  i o panel  which consists of 78 immuno oncology  related targets  and what we saw was that there was a  significant differential  expression between the genes that were  um analyzed between cd19 rich rois  and compared to cd3 rich rois  wherein the targets that were up  regulated in the cd19 which rois  were mainly antigen presenting cell  targets targets like a cd40  cd74 whereas the targets that were  upregulated and enriched in the cd3 rich  regions of interest were mainly t-cell  markers  and chemokines and cytokines now  our cd19 rich regions we expect  are regions that are high in b cells and  cd3 raised regions  are regions that we expect are high in t  cells  so after having analyzed this by digital  spatial profiling  our next step was to validate these  some of the key targets that we analyzed  using rna scope on a serial section  so for that purpose uh we selected roi  6 and roi 11. as you can see roi 6 is  a cd19 rich roi and roi 11 is a cd3 rich  roi  so this way we can compare the  differential gene expression  between these two roi that we got from  our geomets dsp analysis  and then pick certain key targets that  would essentially express  and come back to rna scope to validate  that expression  on a serial section  so the key targets that we pick for  validation  are are targets like cd8 interferon  gamma  cxcl9 and ccl5 which are key  players in the cancer immunity cycle um  and these were differentially expressed  between roi 6 and roi 11.  so using our multiplex  v2 assay we were able to visualize these  targets and compare their expression  between  the cd3 rich roi and the cd19 rich roi  now as you can see in this image uh the  expression of  all of these targets was significantly  higher in the roi 11  compared to roi 6. now roi 11  is the roi that is cd3 rich  or c cell rich and cd and roi  6 is the roi which is cd19 rich or a b  cell rich so it was no surprise that  these targets  which are mainly expressed on t cells  were  expressed at a much higher level in roi  11  compared to roi 6. and it was nice to  see  that our expression pattern uh  was concordant with the dsp data that  you can see in this graph  showing that these two technologies are  comparable and their expression patterns  correlate  with one another with rna scope as i  mentioned earlier you can get that  single molecule and single cell  resolution  so after having identified your key  targets from your dsp data  you can come back and visualize your p  target expression  with morphological and tissue context  so with this joint workflow we really  wanted to address all the questions  in spatial genomics where we've used rna  score  as a molecular guide to identify key  regions  within a heterogeneous tumor then using  the geomets psp panel  we can profile these selected regions of  interest  for target gene expression  in this case targets related to io  and then visualize the key targets that  are  differentially expressed using rna scope  on a serial section  so this way we we're hoping to provide a  complete solution  for spatial genomics combining the  strength of both these technologies  to provide highly flex spatial profiling  with single cell and morphological  resolution  our technology has been widely applied  over the last few years  as you can see we have over 2700  publications  as of last month and we have been used  in various different research areas  but cancer and neuroscience are top  research areas  for publication  in addition to our broad applications in  cancer and neuroscience  we've also widely been applied in  infectious disease research  and in the current environment it's  imperative that we  expedite our research for covert 19  and help identify therapeutic and  vaccine strategies  that will help control this pandemic and  we are trying to contribute to this  by having probes uh for covet 19 that  would specifically identify  this virus and also have probes that  would identify the whole cell receptor  or chemokines cytokines immune cells and  finally  pathological and physiological markers  to study  tissue homeostasis to learn more do not  hesitate  to reach out to our support finally we  have a lot of material  related to oncology and immuno oncology  as you can see on the screen we have  white papers and app nodes  and we are also going to be presenting  four different posters  at the aacr meeting later this month so  please reach out to us with any  questions  uh you can reach out to either of the  email addresses and in the current  environment we know a lot of you cannot  get to your lab  but you still have research and grand  deadlines to meet  so at acd we have a dedicated group of  researchers  who are safely working in our office  to help advance your research we have  pharma assay services  and academic assay services for pharma  and academic customers  where you only have to send your samples  to us  we'll do the early scope analysis for  you do the data analysis  quantification and give the data back to  you  uh in four weeks so if you want to learn  more about these services that we offer  do reach out to us and contact our  support  thank you
 

